From 4c8b8454497c28ff04a93188fc10b5c94a867f07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:31:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let the remote agent decide whether a remote file is writable

Over SSH, Fresh judged a remote file's writability by comparing the
file's uid/gid with the local process's own ids. Those come from
different hosts, so with `auto_read_only` on, a file only its owner may
write was opened read-only whenever the local and remote uids differ
(Termux is one easy way to get there), and the other way round a file
the remote user can't write could look writable (#2944).

The agent's `stat` now reports `writable`, from `os.access(W_OK)` as the
remote user, and the client uses it. An agent that doesn't send it
falls back to the old comparison.

Fixes #2944

Assisted-by: Claude Code
